~ amador_intro
# Intro of the game
Amador: My head.. it [shake]hurts[/shake].
Amador: Wh... What am I doing here? Hold on, isn't this the [shake]basement?[/shake] 
??: [pulse]Look around, Amador[/pulse] 
=> END

~ amador_first_step
# This plays after trying to exit the basement without a key.
% Amador: The door's closed. I should find the key first.
% Amador: It's no use; the door's closed. Where was the key?
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_locker
# This plays after seeing the locker without the key.
% Amador: Hmm...maybe the key is inside the locker.
% Amador: ...wasn't the key in there?
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_first
# This plays after searching the box.
% Amador: There are [color={red}]{text}[/color] clocks inside.
% Amador: Two clocks. Why are there TWO here?.
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_second
# This plays after getting the second number.
The book name is [i]The Big Four[/i].
% Amador: Nice name. Greater book.
% Amador: I should read this sometime.
% Amador: Got it. So close to leaving this [shake]basement[/shake].
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_last
# This plays after getting the last number.
The Painting's name is [i]Composition IX[/i].
% Amador: Great, fantastic painting. Loved it.
% Amador: This painting is... breathtaking.
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_open_locker
# This plays after getting the key and opening the key.
% Amador: So tiny, yet so important.
% Amador: Got the key; let's head basck to the door now.
% Amador: Finally, the key in my hands. Let's go to the door.
=> END

~ amador_tv
# TV machine
Maite: We should clean up the basement; it's a bit messy, after all.
...
...
Maite: And the washimg machine... isn't it broken?? It surely belongs in the trash.
....
Maite: The books do look interesting, though. We are keeping them.
=> END

 ~ amador_open_locker_with_key
# This plays when opening the locker after getting the key.
% Amador: Let's open up the locker.
% Amador: Finally, let's open up this locker.
% Amador: The mistery is over; let's crack this up.
=> END

~ reaccionar_a_pin
if GLOBAL.numpad_input == "123":
	¡Correcto! La puerta se abre.
else:
	Incorrecto. Inténtalo de nuevo.
	do request_numpad()
=> END

~ amador_bookshelf
# Bookshelf
% Amador: So many books in here...no wonder i'm sleeping in the [shake]basement[/shake].
% Amador: There may be something here... in-between this pile of books.
% Amador: Can't see a thing here. Let's go deeper.

- Look inside => amador_first_chain_found_second
- Do nothing => END

~ amador_hidden_painting
# Painting
% Amador: A mistery... I love misteries. Let's unveil it!
% Amador: Wonder what's under... Let's see.

- Look under => amador_first_chain_found_last
- Do nothing => END

~ nothing
Amador: Let's see what we have here... 

% Amador: There is... [rainbow]nothing[/rainbow] here.
% Amador: Hmm, looks like ... [rainbow]nothing's [/rainbow] here.
% Amador: What a bummer.. looks like ...[rainbow]nothing's [/rainbow] here.
% Amador: Amazing!  looks like ... [rainbow]nothing's [/rainbow] here. 
=> END

~ amador_cute_box
# Cute box
% Amador: What a mess...let's open the box.
% Amador: Why did i leve this here?  Maybe opening it will clear that up.
% Amador: I should put this elsewhere. Let's take a look at the contents first.

- Look inside => amador_first_chain_found_first
- Do nothing => END


